      "description": "Contains the main happy-path test scenarios for the Product API, executed in sequential order (S01–S15).\n\nThe flow covers the full lifecycle of both category (api/kategori) and product (api/produk) resources:\n- Create a category and a product (POST)\n- Retrieve a product by ID (GET)\n- Update a product fully or partially (PUT / PATCH)\n- Soft-delete and restore a product (DELETE / PATCH restore)\n- Verify a deleted product returns Not Found (GET)\n- List all products (GET)\n- Attempt to delete a category that is still in use, then create a replacement and hard-delete the original (DELETE)\n- Confirm the deleted category is no longer found (GET)\n\nAll requests in this folder are expected to return successful responses. They are designed to be run in order, as each step may depend on data (IDs, variables) produced by the previous one."
    },
