      "description": "Contains negative test scenarios for the Product API, covering all expected error and validation failure cases (N01–N14).\n\nThe scenarios target both category (api/kategori) and product (api/produk) endpoints and verify that the API correctly rejects invalid or conflicting requests:\n- Missing required fields on POST (category and product)\n- Duplicate category name or duplicate product code\n- Invalid field values on POST, GET, and PATCH\n- Reference to a non-existent category when creating a product\n- Attempting to GET, DELETE, or restore a product that does not exist\n- Double-delete and double-restore attempts on the same product\n\nAll requests in this folder are expected to return error responses (e.g. 400, 404, 422). They validate that the API enforces its business rules and returns clear, consistent error messages under failure conditions."
